From bca99eef6b704af65809af82f9509f0ae37d06e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CC Stage2 <cc@iis.local>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 05:28:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] Site-wide legal fine print: disclaimer strip on every
 page + contextual risk notices

Users following troubleshooting steps, running tools, or acting on data from
iisupp.net now see, in writing, that it is general information used at their own
risk, that it may be out of date, and that they should call us if it matters.

- disclaimer.html: full 14-section Website Content Disclaimer (Ontario law),
  linked from Terms s.9 and the Governance footer. /disclaimer clean URL added.
- assets/iis-fineprint.css: two styles - the site-wide foot strip and a smaller
  contextual notice. Deliberately low-contrast; this is fine print, not a banner.
- scripts/inject-disclaimer.mjs: idempotent codemod, foot strip on all 117 public
  pages. 16 pages skipped by design, each with a stated reason (never silent).
- scripts/inject-riskbar.mjs: contextual notice on the 13 pages where a visitor
  actually executes something. Explicit anchors - fails loudly rather than
  guessing a position.
- scripts/check-disclaimer-coverage.mjs: gate wired into site:hygiene. A new page
  without the notice now turns the build red. Proven red on all three failure
  modes (missing strip, missing notice, hand-edited notice) before trusting it.

Change the wording once in the injector and re-run; the whole site follows.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TAEeWzAz1B7dHt85zVuk8C
