+
+            <p>This Disclaimer governs your use of content published on <strong>iisupp.net</strong> and every associated sub-site, subdomain, forum, knowledge base, downloadable asset, calculator, assessment, AI assistant and application operated by <strong>Integrated IT Support Inc.</strong> ("we", "us", "our"). It applies alongside our <a href="/terms.html">Terms &amp; Conditions</a> and <a href="/governance/privacy">Privacy Notice</a>. By using this site you accept the terms set out below.</p>
+
+            <h3>1. General Information Only</h3>
+            <p>Articles, guides, FAQs, forum posts, knowledge-base entries, checklists, scripts, configuration examples, benchmarks and commentary are published for general informational and educational purposes. They are <strong>not</strong> a substitute for a professional assessment of your own systems, and they do not take into account your hardware, software versions, licensing, network topology, security posture, regulatory obligations or business continuity requirements.</p>
+
+            <h3>2. Use At Your Own Risk</h3>
+            <p>Any troubleshooting procedure, instruction, command, script, registry or configuration change, tool, template or data set obtained from this site is <strong>used entirely at your own risk</strong>. IT environments differ, and a step that is harmless in one environment can cause data loss, downtime, security exposure, licence breach or hardware damage in another.</p>
+            <p>Before you act on anything published here, you are responsible for taking a verified backup, testing in a non-production environment where practical, confirming you have the authority to make the change, and satisfying yourself that the step is appropriate for your circumstances. <strong>We strongly recommend that you do not perform changes on production or business-critical systems without qualified supervision.</strong></p>
+
+            <h3>3. Accuracy and Currency — Content May Be Outdated</h3>
+            <p>Technology, vendor products, security advisories, pricing, regulations and best practice change constantly. Content that was accurate when written <strong>may since have become outdated, superseded or incorrect</strong>, and we do not undertake to review or update it. Publication dates, version numbers and figures shown on this site are indicative only.</p>
+            <p><strong>Please carry out your own due diligence and verify against current vendor documentation and your own environment before relying on any content or data from this site.</strong></p>
+
+            <h3>4. No Professional Advice, No Engagement</h3>
+            <p>Nothing on this site constitutes professional IT, security, legal, regulatory, financial, tax or accounting advice, and nothing on this site creates a client, advisory, retainer or fiduciary relationship between you and Integrated IT Support Inc. A relationship is formed only under a written or electronic confirmation of scope as described in our <a href="/terms.html">Terms &amp; Conditions</a>. Where compliance, privacy or regulatory questions arise, obtain advice from a qualified professional in the relevant jurisdiction.</p>
+
+            <h3>5. Assessments, Calculators, Scores and Estimates</h3>
+            <p>Health checks, readiness assessments, maturity scores, cost calculators, savings estimates, benchmarks and comparison tables produce <strong>indicative, non-binding outputs based on the limited inputs supplied</strong>. They are not audits, penetration tests, certifications, valuations or formal quotations, and they must not be presented to a third party as evidence of compliance or certification. Actual pricing is confirmed only in a written proposal.</p>
+
+            <h3>6. AI-Generated and Automated Content</h3>
+            <p>Parts of this site — including ARIA, in-page assistants, automated summaries and generated knowledge-base entries — produce content automatically. Automated systems can be <strong>incomplete, out of date, or confidently wrong</strong>. Treat every automated response as a starting point to be verified, never as a final answer, and never as a basis for an irreversible action. See our <a href="/governance/ai-use.html">AI Use Notice</a>.</p>
+
+            <h3>7. Community, Forum and Third-Party Content</h3>
+            <p>Forum posts, community answers, user submissions and comments reflect the views of their authors, not Integrated IT Support Inc. We do not verify, endorse or warrant such content. Links to third-party websites, vendors, downloads and documentation are provided for convenience only; we do not control and are not responsible for their content, availability, security or terms.</p>
+
+            <h3>8. Software and Downloads</h3>
+            <p>Any application, extension, installer, script or file made available through this site is provided <strong>"as is" and without warranty of any kind</strong>. You are responsible for scanning, validating and testing anything you download, and for confirming it is compatible with and appropriate for your systems and your organisation's policies.</p>
+
+            <h3>9. No Warranty</h3>
+            <p>To the fullest extent permitted by applicable law, all content on this site is provided <strong>"as is" and "as available", without warranties or conditions of any kind</strong>, whether express, implied or statutory, including without limitation any implied warranty of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, accuracy, completeness, currency, uninterrupted availability or non-infringement. We do not warrant that this site or any content will be error-free or that defects will be corrected.</p>
+
+            <h3>10. Limitation of Liability</h3>
